  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_032 (multimodal, scvi_n200, resnet50, multiprofile, transformer, concat) is our best result at 0.688 acc, a ~3.5% gain over RNA-only multiprofile (0.653). However, image-only with resnet50 is very poor (0.208 acc), raising the question of whether resnet50 is a bottleneck limiting the image's contribution in fusion. Question: config_038 changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings identical to config_032, cleanly isolating the effect of image encoder quality on multimodal performance. Why this is the best next experiment: It is a single-variable comparison to our current best, tests a high-impact design decision (whether a stronger image representation unlocks substantially more complementary signal), and the answer will determine whether further investment in image encoder quality is worthwhile or whether the image modality's contribution is fundamentally limited regardless of encoder choice. This is more informative than testing minor architectural variants (e.g., concat vs. weighted fusion) under the current budget constraints."
}

